---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Create a project under an explicit original operation identity

Usage: pse project create [OPTIONS] --reader <READER> --state <STATE> --issuing-store <ISSUING_STORE> --operation <OPERATION> <PROJECT> <TITLE>

Arguments:
  <PROJECT>  Canonical project key
  <TITLE>    Human-readable project title

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --reader <READER>                Exact reader identifier returned by `pse observe prepare`
      --format <FORMAT>                Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --state <STATE>                  Exact existing private canonical deployment state directory
      --database <DATABASE>            Exact existing database; defaults to the database configured by the deployment
      --fields <FIELDS>                Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --budget <BUDGET>                Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --timeout-ms <TIMEOUT_MS>        Total reader allowance in milliseconds, from 1 through 25000
      --issuing-store <ISSUING_STORE>  Expected issuing store reported by the original project read
      --operation <OPERATION>          Original operation identity, retained across acknowledgement queries
  -h, --help                           Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Create a project under an explicit original operation identity

Usage: pse project create [OPTIONS] --reader <READER> --state <STATE> --issuing-store <ISSUING_STORE> --operation <OPERATION> <PROJECT> <TITLE>

Arguments:
  <PROJECT>
          Canonical project key

  <TITLE>
          Human-readable project title

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --reader <READER>
          Exact reader identifier returned by `pse observe prepare`

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --state <STATE>
          Exact existing private canonical deployment state directory

      --database <DATABASE>
          Exact existing database; defaults to the database configured by the deployment

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --timeout-ms <TIMEOUT_MS>
          Total reader allowance in milliseconds, from 1 through 25000

      --issuing-store <ISSUING_STORE>
          Expected issuing store reported by the original project read

      --operation <OPERATION>
          Original operation identity, retained across acknowledgement queries

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
